Build the backend for my existing DevFix AI project using Node.js + Express.

IMPORTANT:
Create ONLY the normal core/business backend.
Do NOT implement LangChain, LangGraph, AI agents, FastAPI, or GitHub OAuth yet.

TECH STACK:
- Node.js
- Express.js
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM
- JWT authentication
- bcrypt
- dotenv
- CORS
- Helmet
- Morgan

PROJECT STRUCTURE:

backend/
├── src/
│   ├── config/
│   ├── controllers/
│   ├── middleware/
│   ├── routes/
│   ├── services/
│   ├── utils/
│   ├── app.js
│   └── server.js
├── prisma/
│   └── schema.prisma
├── .env.example
├── package.json
└── README.md

CREATE THESE MODULES:

1. Authentication
- Register
- Login
- JWT authentication
- Get current user

2. Users
- User profile
- Update profile

3. Repositories
Create CRUD APIs for repositories.
Fields:
- id
- name
- fullName
- owner
- url
- language
- description
- openIssues
- createdAt
- updatedAt

4. Issues
Create APIs for issues.
Fields:
- id
- repositoryId
- issueNumber
- title
- description
- status
- priority
- labels
- createdAt
- updatedAt

5. Agent Runs
Create database/API structure for future AI runs.
Fields:
- id
- issueId
- status
- currentAgent
- progress
- confidence
- rootCause
- createdAt
- updatedAt

6. Pull Requests
Fields:
- id
- issueId
- title
- url
- status
- filesChanged
- linesAdded
- linesRemoved
- createdAt

7. Approvals
Fields:
- id
- agentRunId
- status
- reviewerId
- reviewedAt

8. Activity Logs
Store important system/agent events.

API ROUTES:

/api/auth
/api/users
/api/repositories
/api/issues
/api/agent-runs
/api/pull-requests
/api/approvals
/api/activity

REQUIREMENTS:
- Proper MVC/service architecture
- Central error handling
- Request validation
- Authentication middleware
- Protected routes where required
- Environment variables
- Clean async/await code
- Consistent JSON responses
- HTTP status codes
- No hardcoded secrets

Also create:
GET /api/health

Return:
{
  "status": "ok",
  "service": "devfix-core"
}

Use PostgreSQL through Prisma.

Keep the implementation simple and production-ready.
Do not add unnecessary features.